{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>To whom do you belong.</b> Whose are you — who sent you? And the Targum renders: דְּמָן אַתְּ?" "<b>And whose are these before you.</b> These that are before you — whose are they? To whom is this gift sent? The letter lamed serves at the head of the word in place of 'of/belonging to', as in: ״וְכֹל אֲשֶׁר אַתָּה רֹאֶה לִי הוּא״ (Genesis 31:43) — 'is mine'; ״לַה' הָאָרֶץ וּמְלוֹאָהּ״ (Psalms 24) — 'is HaShem's.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:46.379063183Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}